            "state": "Texas",
            "priority": 1,
            "description": "<p>John Connally's political life has been defined by him waiting in the wings, lifting up other men of history in their time of need, Johnson, Nixon, he even helped get Ike into the game. In 1980, however, he's chosen to take the spotlight for himself, America needs someone to bring it back from the brink, and to Connally, there's no-one better suited to the task than him.</p><p>The battle for the nomination alone has been an uphill battle, taking down Reagan is certain to leave some harsh wounds within the party, and many Republican's still don't fully think of him as one of their own, but he's made it to the helm, and only a stable vessel can carry him to victory against Jimmy Carter.",
